From bed99d1afe1322822737b4f2edaeb46241c21a1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 090/101] sunxi: h713: hy300pro_g_eu_defconfig, the
 HY300PRO-G-EU's own board base

The maintainer's own HY300 Pro (box label HY300PRO-G-EU, stock Android 11 of
2025-05-06) is not the HY300 Pro of issue #1, and hy300_pro_defconfig (636
MHz) is not its base. Its own boot0 at LBA 16 (eMMC dump of 2026-10-02) holds
the 24 DRAM words hy310_defconfig boots with, except tpr0..tpr2, which the
DDR3 arm of iw12_set_timing() returns before reading.

So this is hy310_defconfig with four lines changed and nothing else: the
device tree and the identification string name the board, and tpr0..tpr2
are this board's own words instead of the bench board's. The only symbol
hy310_defconfig does not set, CONFIG_IDENT_STRING, is the one
hy300_pro_defconfig already sets.

No image is shipped from this base; the board is profile-only and gets the
stage 5 test image. Built by nobody yet: a kconfig run and a build are the
integrator's (package GEU1 checked the setting lines with diff only).
---
 configs/hy300pro_g_eu_defconfig | 98 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 98 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 configs/hy300pro_g_eu_defconfig

diff --git a/configs/hy300pro_g_eu_defconfig b/configs/hy300pro_g_eu_defconfig
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..b8fd7c18a91
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/hy300pro_g_eu_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+# HY300PRO-G-EU -- board base. The maintainer's own HY300 Pro (box label
+# HY300PRO-G-EU, stock Android 11 of 2025-05-06). It is NOT the HY300 Pro of
+# issue #1 (hy300_pro_defconfig: 636 MHz, another firmware family).
+#
+# Same shape as hy310_defconfig, and hy310_defconfig line for line except four
+# things: the device tree, the identification string, and tpr0..tpr2. This
+# board is HY310-like where it has been measured: its vendor boot0 at LBA 16
+# (h713-install dump, 2026-10-02) carries the HY310's DRAM words except tpr13,
+# and its tpr13 0xb4016103 is the value this defconfig family already boots
+# with. A role fragment in configs/fragments/ says what a build is for, and
+# build/uboot-build.sh merges the two (docs/uboot/README.md).
+#
+# **No image is shipped for this board.** It is profile-only
+# (boards/hy300pro-g-eu/README.md): nobody has run our firmware on it. The only
+# build this base is meant for is the stage 5 test image (`--test-image`).
+#
+# Where the DRAM values come from:
+#   - clk 792, type 3, zq, odt_en, para1, para2, mr0..mr3, tpr3..tpr13: this
+#     board's own boot0 words, and equal to hy310_defconfig's.
+#   - tpr0..tpr2 0x004a2195/0x02423190/0x0008b061: this board's own boot0 words
+#     (hy310_defconfig carries the bench board's 0x00482151/0x01b1a94c/
+#     0x0006e04d). Neither reaches the hardware: the DDR3 arm of
+#     iw12_set_timing() in arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50iw12.c returns before
+#     the only code that unpacks tpr0..tpr2 (the LPDDR3 arm).
+#   - DX_ODT, DX_DRI, CA_DRI are not among the 24 boot0 words; they are the
+#     value every H713 defconfig carries, and dram_sun50iw12.c does not read
+#     them.
+#   - The project id is not here: h713-install writes h713_project from the
+#     board's own panel_config.ini (0x34) into the environment.
+CONFIG_ARM=y
+CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300pro-g-eu"
+CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=792
+CONFIG_SPL=y
+CONFIG_IDENT_STRING=" HY300PRO-G-EU"
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_ODT=0x03030303
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_DRI=0x0e0e0e0e
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_CA_DRI=0x1c12
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_ODT_EN=0x1
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_ZQ=0x007b7bfb
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_PARA1=0x000010f4
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_PARA2=0x04000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR0=0x00001c70
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR1=0x00000040
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR2=0x00000018
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR3=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR0=0x004a2195
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR1=0x02423190
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR2=0x0008b061
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR3=0xb4787896
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR4=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR5=0x48484848
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR6=0x00000048
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR7=0x1620121e
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR8=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR9=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR10=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR11=0x44340000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR12=0x00006666
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR13=0xb4016103
+CONFIG_MACH_SUN50I_H713=y
+CONFIG_H713_POWERON_LIGHT_FAN=y
+CONFIG_H713_MIPS_BOOT=y
+CONFIG_SUNXI_DRAM_H713_DDR3_STOCK=y
+CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA=2
+CONFIG_MMC0_CD_PIN=""
+CONFIG_MMC_HS200_SUPPORT=y
+# CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
+CONFIG_SUPPORT_EMMC_BOOT=y
+CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
+CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
+# CONFIG_WATCHDOG is not set
+CONFIG_WDT=y
+CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
+CONFIG_CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE=y
+# CONFIG_USB_ETHER is not set
+CONFIG_CONSOLE_MUX=y
+CONFIG_SYS_CONSOLE_IS_IN_ENV=y
+CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ACM=y
+# CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ACM_WAIT_FOR_CONNECTION is not set
+CONFIG_SYSRESET=y
+CONFIG_SYSRESET_PSCI=y
+CONFIG_CMD_POWEROFF=y
+CONFIG_FASTBOOT_CMD_OEM_POWEROFF=y
+# No "usb start" in the preboot: the host-side USB scan cost 2 to 5 s on every
+# boot and nothing in the product boot reads a USB device (no keyboard, no USB
+# boot medium; the installer role uses the gadget, not the host). The two
+# reboot-mode magics stay: "reboot fastboot" and "reboot bootloader" from Linux.
+CONFIG_PREBOOT="if itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xfa57b007; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; run fastboot_mode; elif itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xb007c0de; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; setenv bootdelay -1; fi"
+# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT is not set
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC=y
+CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET=0x700000
+CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=1
+CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x800
+CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_DATA_PART_OFFSET=0x0
+CONFIG_H713_VENDOR_CHAINLOAD=y
+CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y
+CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
